{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1462434546,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDY1MTE3MzUzMA=="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1462434546,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDY1MTE3MzUzMQ=="},"added":["do-in-datalad"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1462435437,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxNzA5NzU5Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/424#issuecomment-217097597"},"message":"Quick follow up:\n\nThis workaround could be extended to also address a similar issue, namely when the submodule is actually checked out at its configured mountpoint inside the parent repository. In this case, we could attempt to clone from a URL that we derive from the origin URL and the `path` setting in `.gitmodules` using the same logic.\n\nIt could be argued that checking such a URL first would be better than going to the configured source URL for the submodule. Rational: if the parent repo actually contains an accessible checkout of its submodule, it is more likely to actually contain the desired commit.\n\nIf we want to do this, the workaround presented above would need to be modified to skip the initial \"blind\" clone attempt and pre-configure a candidate submodule URL. Here are the steps for the same URL as above (other initial candidate URLs are possible, obviously):\n\n```\n% datalad install -s http://psydata.ovgu.de/studyforrest/templatetransforms/.git tnt\n1 installed item is available at\n\u003cDataset path=/tmp/tnt\u003e\n% cd tnt\n% git config submodule.raw/structural.url http://psydata.ovgu.de/studyforrest/structural/.git/\n% datalad install raw/structural\n2016-05-05 10:01:39,107 [ERROR  ] stderr| Cloning into 'raw/structural'... (cmd.py:351)\n1 installed item is available at\n\u003cDataset path=/tmp/tnt/raw/structural\u003e\n% git -C raw/structural status\nHEAD detached at 54e555a\nnothing to commit, working directory clean\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1462449554,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxNzEzNjE1OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/424#issuecomment-217136158"},"message":"There was some discussion with git upstream: http://thread.gmane.org/gmane.comp.version-control.git/292032 . So indeed rewrites of urls in failed to initialize submodules is a workaround, and indeed might \"scale\" then to similar manual labor for cloning from non-bare clones (i.e. our installations).  I am still not sure though, if there would be any benefit, since such manual url derivation is to be done anyways, to imho more straightforward \"derive url; git clone url submodule/path; git submodule update --init submodule/path\" as I have suggested on the datalad-team ml.\nMeanwhile I think that git should address upstream the issue that it auto-detects/senses .git/ for ssh and local file targets but not http:// repos. I will raise the discussion on git upstream ml","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1462521470,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxNzM3NDIyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/424#issuecomment-217374220"},"message":"Good point. I agree that treating submodule installation like regular cloning (plus subsequent init) has potential to uniformize procedures und we could factor out the relevant bits.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1462545089,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxNzQ1NjA3Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/424#issuecomment-217456077"},"message":"FWIW:  http://thread.gmane.org/gmane.comp.version-control.git/293777  post to git upstream about possibility to sense for /.git over http","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1462556222,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxNzUwOTIzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/424#issuecomment-217509233"},"message":"For now I have crafted apache2 rewrite rule which I have deployed on datasets.datalad.org, so we could approach this workaround path and/or use it for demos if by then no proper resolution is done:\n\n```\n RewriteEngine On\n RewriteCond \"!.*/\\.git/.*\"\n RewriteRule \"(.*?/)((?\u003c!\\.git/)(HEAD|config|annex/objects/.*|objects/(info/[^/]+|[0-9a-f]{2}/[0-9a-f]{38}|pack/pack-[0-9a-f]{40}.(pack|idx))|git-(upload|receive)-pack)|info/refs)$\" \"$1.git/$2\" [PT]\n```\n\nNB ds00005 is indeed not there yet  or smth, so ignore\n\n```\n$\u003e git clone --recursive http://datasets.datalad.org/openfmri\nCloning into 'openfmri'...\nChecking connectivity... done.\nSubmodule 'ds000001' (http://datasets.datalad.org/openfmri/ds000001) registered for path 'ds000001'\nSubmodule 'ds000002' (http://datasets.datalad.org/openfmri/ds000002) registered for path 'ds000002'\nSubmodule 'ds000003' (http://datasets.datalad.org/openfmri/ds000003) registered for path 'ds000003'\nSubmodule 'ds000005' (http://datasets.datalad.org/openfmri/ds000005) registered for path 'ds000005'\n...\nChecking connectivity... done.\nSubmodule path 'ds000003': checked out '6785d552f8949afed4417ed50edf40e5b11fae70'\nCloning into 'ds000005'...\nfatal: repository 'http://datasets.datalad.org/openfmri/ds000005/' not found\nfatal: clone of 'http://datasets.datalad.org/openfmri/ds000005' into submodule path 'ds000005' failed\n\n$\u003e git clone http://datasets.datalad.org/test                \nCloning into 'test'...\nChecking connectivity... done.\n\n$\u003e cd test\n123@  sub1/\n\n$\u003e git annex get 123                         \n(merging origin/git-annex into git-annex...)\n(recording state in git...)\n/tmp/test/.git/annex/tmp/SHA256E-s4--181210f8f9c779c26da1d9b2075b 100%[============================================================================================================================================================\u003e]       4  --.-KB/s    in 0s      \n(checksum...) ok\n(recording state in git...)\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1462958875,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxODQwNzk2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/424#issuecomment-218407960"},"message":"FTR: PR 427 fully implements a solution to this issue.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1462964567,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxODQyNzc4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/424#issuecomment-218427784"},"message":"All merged now, closing....","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1462964570,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50NjU3MDAzMDAw"},"status":2}]}